  <section|Actual public binding><label|actual-public-binding>

  <block|<tformat|<twith|table-width|1par>|<twith|table-hmode|exact>|<cwith|1|-1|1|-1|cell-hyphen|t>|<cwith|1|1|1|-1|cell-bborder|1ln>|<cwith|1|1|1|-1|cell-valign|bottom>|<table|<row|<cell|<strong|Manuscript
  step>>|<cell|<strong|Exact source declaration>>|<cell|<strong|Source path
  and checked role>>>|<row|<cell|Public theorem
  caller>|<cell|<verbatim|YM.Independent.constructionRun>>|<cell|<verbatim|Lean/YM/Independent/ConstructionRun.lean>;
  uses the native preselected postnumeric period selector, not a separate
  grantor route.>>|<row|<cell|Native selector>|<cell|<verbatim|YM.PhysicalNext.Repeat.Legato.R2I.RG05Joint.selectRunWithTreasuryPeriod_preselected_quote_orders_postnumeric_of_prediction>>|<cell|<verbatim|Lean/YM/Integration/NativePreselectedPostnumericPeriodRun.lean>;
  selects the Run, its campaign parameter and funded certificate, while
  preserving the postnumeric preselection.>>|<row|<cell|Common
  campaign/period package>|<cell|<verbatim|YM.PhysicalNext.Repeat.Legato.R2I.RG05Joint.allFactorWithTreasuryPeriod_preselected_quote_orders_postnumeric_of_prediction>,
  <verbatim|YM.PhysicalNext.Repeat.Legato.R2I.RG05Joint.plentifulWithPrediction>,
  <verbatim|YM.PhysicalNext.Repeat.Legato.R2I.RG05Joint.richFaresWithPrediction>>|<cell|<verbatim|Lean/YM/Integration/NativePreselectedPostnumericPeriodClock.lean>,
  <verbatim|RG05Preconstruction/Bardo.lean>, and <verbatim|Fares.lean>. These
  construct the campaign/period inputs before the later selected-run
  attachment. Do not describe the schedule as chosen after <verbatim|rodB>;
  the schedule is independent of the subsequently selected run
  witness.>>|<row|<cell|Original selected configuration and nesting
  receipt>|<cell|<verbatim|YM.PhysicalNext.Repeat.Legato.R2I.RG05Joint.engageWithCustodyFactor>>|<cell|<verbatim|Lean/YM/Integration/RG05Preconstruction/PeriodConstruction.lean>.
  <verbatim|FullVolume.rodB> selects Bolt <verbatim|Y> and a chosen
  certificate whose <verbatim|receipts> give nesting data for <verbatim|Y>.
  The source also chooses the reference schedule, derives branches on
  <verbatim|Y.history>, calls <verbatim|Bandage.coming>, and builds the Run
  using these same data. The campaign is a distinct parameter from the
  Bolt.>>|<row|<cell|Uniform finite-volume
  construction>|<cell|<verbatim|YM.PhysicalNext.Repeat.Legato.Bandage.coming>>|<cell|<verbatim|Lean/YM/FullVolume/Gables/Pillar.lean>.
  Returns one transfer function over all <verbatim|(d,N,p)>, regularity on
  the same trail, and finite-volume witnesses whenever <verbatim|t d \<leq\>
  N>; the cutoff-failure branch uses a default map and does not choose
  another history.>>|<row|<cell|Branch/transition
  data>|<cell|<verbatim|YM.PhysicalNext.Repeat.Legato.Bandage.ease>,
  <verbatim|YM.PhysicalNext.Repeat.Legato.Bandage.Boutique.taste>>|<cell|<verbatim|Lean/YM/FullVolume/Gables/Pillar.lean>.
  Branch data are selected on the original <verbatim|Y.history>; transition
  records are taken from the selected branch.>>|<row|<cell|Funded
  continuation and actual public outputs>|<cell|<verbatim|YM.PhysicalNext.Repeat.Legato.R2I.Funded.gallery>,
  <verbatim|YM.PhysicalNext.Repeat.Legato.R2I.Funded.coverage>;
  <verbatim|YM.PhysicalNext.Repeat.Legato.Run.again>>|<cell|<verbatim|Lean/YM/R2I/Campaign/Accepted.lean>;
  <verbatim|Lean/YM/FullVolume/Cross.lean>. The funded application supplies
  the exact fields <verbatim|R.T>, <verbatim|R.tuning.receipts>,
  <verbatim|R.t>, <verbatim|R.accepts>, <verbatim|R.stories>,
  <verbatim|R.doors>, <verbatim|R.makes>, <verbatim|R.carries>,
  <verbatim|R.books>. Gallery/coverage and the returned centered service and
  Fridge are on <verbatim|R.family>.>>|<row|<cell|Final public
  theorem>|<cell|<verbatim|YM.Nonperturbative.continuum_with_position_tests>>|<cell|<verbatim|Lean/YM/Nonperturbative/Continuum.lean>.
  Its funded goals refine the <verbatim|R,T,W> returned by
  <verbatim|constructionRun>; no second run is constructed.>>>>>

  The selected reference schedule is obtained earlier in the clock/period
  construction than the later <verbatim|rodB> choice. This is logically
  compatible because the schedule is an independent input; the manuscript
  claims only that the resulting schedule and selected history are the ones
  stored together in the Run, not that source execution chooses them in the
  opposite order.

  <section|Service and same-family correspondence><label|service-and-same-family-correspondence>

  <block|<tformat|<twith|table-width|1par>|<twith|table-hmode|exact>|<cwith|1|-1|1|-1|cell-hyphen|t>|<cwith|1|1|1|-1|cell-bborder|1ln>|<cwith|1|1|1|-1|cell-valign|bottom>|<table|<row|<cell|<strong|Manuscript
  step>>|<cell|<strong|Exact source declaration>>|<cell|<strong|Source path
  and checked role>>>|<row|<cell|Core service
  package>|<cell|<verbatim|YM.PhysicalNext.Repeat.Legato.Chateau>>|<cell|<verbatim|Lean/YM/MergeProof/Almandine.lean>;
  retains openings, nesting, nonlinear-response and adjacent-scale bounds,
  transition records, and finite-volume witnesses, with service outputs on
  the family built from the trail/schedule/transfers.>>|<row|<cell|Core
  assembly versus actual funded callback>|<cell|<verbatim|YM.PhysicalNext.Repeat.Legato.chaletrail>;
  <verbatim|YM.PhysicalNext.Repeat.Legato.hearthstone>>|<cell|<verbatim|Lean/YM/MergeProof/Inns.lean>;
  <verbatim|Lean/YM/FullVolume/Hearth.lean>. The former is core service
  assembly. The actual funded callback is the strengthened hearthstone route
  returning centered service, Fridge and Hearthside from the same supplied
  data. Neither chooses a new history.>>|<row|<cell|Centered-service
  construction>|<cell|<verbatim|YM.PhysicalNext.Repeat.Legato.Bandage.nectar>>|<cell|<verbatim|Lean/YM/MergeProof/Gist.lean>.
  Uses the same nesting, transition, campaign, scale and finite-volume data
  for escape, room/bank, scale, height and terminal
  estimates.>>|<row|<cell|Height conversion>|<cell|<verbatim|YM.PhysicalNext.Repeat.Legato.Bandage.resides>>|<cell|<verbatim|Lean/YM/MergeProof/Stove.lean>;
  cross-referenced in <verbatim|prop:ex-geyser-service-fields>.>>|<row|<cell|Adjacent-scale
  input>|<cell|<verbatim|YM.PhysicalNext.Repeat.Legato.Bandage.hiss>,
  <verbatim|YM.PhysicalNext.Repeat.Legato.Bandage.stamina>>|<cell|<verbatim|Lean/YM/MergeProof/Kettle.lean>,
  <verbatim|Lean/YM/MergeProof/Stove.lean>; quantified estimates and the
  common threshold are in <verbatim|thm:ex-selected-geyser-steam> of
  <verbatim|centered-geyser-scale-estimates.tex>. That chapter leaves
  purchased profile/menu estimates and the selected nonlinear response
  explicit.>>|<row|<cell|Relay/transition
  estimates>|<cell|<verbatim|YM.PhysicalNext.Repeat.Legato.Bandage.ravine>>|<cell|<verbatim|Lean/YM/MergeProof/Ravine.lean>;
  uses the same nesting/transition data plus the tariff-based column-rate
  bound.>>|<row|<cell|Terminal marked estimate>|<cell|<verbatim|YM.MergeProof.inviting>,
  <verbatim|YM.MergeProof.Cream>, <verbatim|YM.MergeProof.figment>,
  <verbatim|YM.MergeProof.solaris>>|<cell|<verbatim|Lean/YM/MergeProof/Parterre.lean>,
  <verbatim|Biscuit.lean>, <verbatim|Figment.lean>, and
  <verbatim|Canopy.lean>. <verbatim|inviting> is conditional on soundness,
  reference-level eligibility, union-stencil fit, nonnegative credit, keeper,
  regional card/allowance and cover bounds, the storm bound, positive
  terminal weight and nonnegative reserve. The terminal marked-field work is
  cross-referenced to <verbatim|sec:terminal-marked-construction> and
  <verbatim|sec:ex-marked-field-local>; <verbatim|solaris> supplies these
  conditions eventually in the cutoff for each fixed grade/section in the
  purchased portfolio, uniformly in the period, not for every finite cutoff
  or uniformly over all grades at once.>>>>>

  The family stored in the Run and the family used by its funded continuation
  have identical trail, schedule, transfer function, holonomy, frames and
  sections. The continuation's output is consequently on the selected family
  itself. The proof does not rely on the unrelated grantor entry point or on
  <verbatim|Marco.squad>; <verbatim|Bandage.coming> is the selected uniform
  transfer construction.

  <section|Remaining dependencies and limits><label|remaining-dependencies-and-limits>

  <\itemize-minus>
    <item>The attachment starts from the actual selected funded certificate.
    The common funded-history and three-card chapters supply the shared
    history/campaign and local algebra; this unit does not repeat those
    proofs or claim to reprove all numerical purchases.

    <item>The adjacent-scale chapter proves its arithmetic conversion but
    retains the purchased profile/menu inputs and nonlinear response as
    explicit dependencies.

    <item>The terminal marked estimate is eventual in the cutoff for each
    fixed grade and section of the purchased portfolio, uniformly over
    period. Its hypotheses come from the marked-field-local-estimates
    producer (section label <verbatim|sec:ex-marked-field-local>), including
    the terminal marked-address construction. It is not a consequence of
    centered service alone.

    <item>No external literature result is used. No Lean or LaTeX build was
    run. All text remains draft pending independent review.
  </itemize-minus>

  <section|Checks recorded><label|checks-recorded>

  Inspected source with targeted <verbatim|sed>/<verbatim|rg> commands in the
  assigned clone and checked the exact upstream pin. No Lean files changed.
  <verbatim|git diff --check> passed. <verbatim|python3
  scripts/check_blueprint.py> was run and stopped because this clone has no
  <verbatim|blueprint/units/YM-000026/unit.json>; no checker pass is claimed.
  No Lean or LaTeX build and no test command was run.

